  <running_head>De Duellis.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>ad-</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">peramento tale duellum ap-</l>
    <l n="2">probandum videtur, si respu-</l>
    <l n="3">blica legitimum bellum gerat,</l>
    <l n="4">si satis virium non habeat, ut</l>
    <l n="5">hosti potenti resistat, resque sit</l>
    <l n="6">desperata, nisi tale duellum su-</l>
    <l n="7">scipiatur, in quo ea respublica</l>
    <l n="8">superior censebitur, cujus pro-</l>
    <l n="9">pugnator victoriam reporta-</l>
    <l n="10">verit. Exemplum hujus illu-</l>
    <l n="11">stre occurrit in historiis Go-</l>
    <l n="12">thorum Suenonumque. Cum</l>
    <l n="13">enim Gramus Danorum Rex S-</l>
    <l n="14">cariae Gothorum Regis po-</l>
    <l n="15">tentiam formidaret, adeo ut</l>
    <l n="16">eum superari non posse, crede-</l>
    <l n="17">ret, à singulari certamine præ-</l>
    <l n="18">sidium opportunum mutuari</l>
    <l n="19">constituit; in quo Gothorum</l>
    <l n="20">rege interfecto rem Sueciae nu-</l>
    <l n="21">tantem fecit, ac fere despera-</l>
    <l n="22">tam.</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">Neque obstat, quod[?] non vi-</l>
    <l n="24">deatur tantum negotium col-</l>
    <l n="25">locandum esse in capite unius.</l>
    <l n="26">Quia non aliter hoc duellum</l>
  </main_text>
  <marginalia>
    <note side="right" at="peramento tale duellum" line_from="1" line_to="1">Azor.In-stit.Mo-ral.part. 3. libr.2. cap.5.</note>
    <note side="right" at="Exemplum hujus illustre" line_from="10" line_to="10">Johan. Magnus Goth. Hi-stor. libr. 11.</note>
  </marginalia>
  <notes>The second paragraph is cut off at the foot of the page; its continuation is on the next page. The reading "quod" in the second paragraph has a doubtful mark over the u, so it is marked [?]. The marginal notes have no reference marks in the text, so each note is placed beside the line where it begins. The catchword "ad-" is the first word of the next page.</notes>
